"Intake houses new Avowed teens on Anesidora who are not going straight into a school."
"Registration starts a pre-arrival guide; many spend their last three months with family."
"On arrival an Avowed-trauma therapist decides between the intake dorms and monitoring."
"Towers group classes: Rabbits with Shapers, Healers, Meisters and Adjusters; Brutes apart."
"U-types keep their own floor and do not mingle; Sways live in a low brick building."
"Suites get talking-point features like pinball machines to encourage socializing."
"Counselors of the same class guide each floor, with volunteer buddies for newcomers."
"Activities fill 6 AM to a loose midnight curfew; half earn credits that must be met."
"Overstaying intake by weeks past about two months gets a resident put out."
"Newcomers may not teleport in guests from home for their first few months."
"The rule guards against homesickness, family trouble, hangers-on and anti-alien cultists."
"The Rabbit floors are called the Warren."
